| **LOW (risk)** | plan.md:43 | The review question is already answered by the design: no compatibility mode. cat.md:1189-1191 calls the nil rule "a deliberate execution-contract change from today's zipmap fallback", and contract `"v2"` is amended in place before first publication (cat.md:655). Today's fallthrough is `resolve-var` env → store → primitives → modules (`engine.cljc:46-58`) and `(zipmap params [])` on zero-arg calls (`ast_walker.cljc:511`). The whole parity corpus is name-based, e.g. `binop` builds `{:type :variable :name op}` for operators (`semantic_stream_observer_test.cljc:52-56`), which must become `:global`. | Enforce strictly. Add a corpus audit to the plan: every `:variable` with a free name becomes `:global`, every lambda gains `:arity`. |
